From 82428410ca486598446fe9ff21dfd2c4f7ca3926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viljo Marrandi <30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:52:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(app,ui): a refused generation marks the spot it
 names

#261 part 2, by the triage's middle ground: a refusal does not draw a
partial path, it draws the place it is about. A generator refusal can
carry one spot (GenError::At, built with GenError::invalid_at); run_job
carries it to world through the op's frame, the generate command keeps
it (CommandError::MachiningAt), and the UI marks it in the viewport with
a gouge-coloured cross while the refusal stands. The op page's refusal
line becomes a link that frames it. Nothing is generated or cached, so
nothing refused can post. The located errors read exactly like the
plain ones, so no message changes.

First adopters are the refusals that already quoted a point: Face's
narrow strip between two holes, the drill cycle's R-plane, counterbore,
bore-fit and centre-cutting doors, Bore's and Thread's counterbore and
fit doors, and the plunge law. The cross-hole spindle frame moves the
spot by the same shift it applies to the sentence.

GenError moves to machining2d/gen_error.rs (face.rs re-exports it).

Refs #261

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
